{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "29", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "44", "S": "33"}}, "news": [{"title": "Don\u2019t issue completion certificates to buildings in aquifer zones: Madras HC tells GCC", "para": "The Madras High Court has mandated the Greater Chennai Corporation to impose strict regulations on Aquifer Recharge Zones, which include Kottivakkam, Palavakkam, and Uthandi. Construction activities in these areas will now be under vigilant scrutiny, highlighting the importance of following the Tamil Nadu Combined Development and Building Rules. A dedicated monitoring committee will be tasked with overseeing development and ensuring all future permits comply with these essential regulations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/dont-issue-completion-certificates-to-buildings-in-aquifer-zones-madras-hc-tells-gcc/135289658?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-67598/135289658.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Noida authority board adopts model building regulations to remove FAR cap", "para": "The Noida Authority has green-lighted the implementation of the Model Building Regulations, 2026, aimed at transforming urban landscapes. With the removal of the FAR cap for group housing along extensive 45-metre roadways, high-rise structures are set to gain momentum. Moreover, a master developer for the envisioned AI City-cum-Business Park will be appointed via competitive bidding.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/noida-authority-board-adopts-model-building-regulations-to-remove-far-cap/135289157?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-202984/135289157.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Keralam orders vigilance probe into KIIFB land acquisition in Kannur", "para": "The Kerala government's Cabinet convened to decide on a thorough inquiry into the land acquisition practices of KIIFB. This probe stems from Chief Minister V D Satheesan's concerns raised within the Assembly. An expert panel highlighted issues related to the acquisition of almost 1,000 acres in Kannur, suggesting that the purchased land was unsuitable for construction and obtained at inflated rates.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/keralam-orders-vigilance-probe-into-kiifb-land-acquisition-in-kannur/135288647?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-128712/135288647.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}